L["The plate under your mouse ignores Non-target opacity and range fading, so you can always read it."] = "The plate under your mouse ignores Non-target opacity and range fading, so you can always read it."
L["The plate under your mouse is drawn above every other plate, so you can read it in a stack. Beats Casting enemies in front and your target."] = "The plate under your mouse is drawn above every other plate, so you can read it in a stack. Beats Casting enemies in front and your target."
L["The preview"] = "The preview"
L["The preview at the top of the window is a sample enemy nameplate that updates as you change settings. The part you are editing is outlined.\n\nThe preview shows what your settings turn on: raid icons, quest icons, auras, absorbs, the power bar and more appear when they are enabled and disappear when they are not. The Target, Focus and Mouseover pages show the sample in that state, and Buff warnings shows its warnings.\n\nA few pages have a Preview button next to Reset this section for things the sample can't tell from your settings: on the Cast bar page it picks the cast the preview plays, on the Health bar page it picks the sample's enemy type and threat, and on the Elite icon page it picks the badge. They only change the preview, are never saved, and go back to their default when you leave the page.\n\nPages that only matter in the world, like the Behavior pages and Game settings, say so under the preview."] = "The preview at the top of the window is a sample enemy nameplate that updates as you change settings. The part you are editing is outlined.\n\nThe preview shows what your settings turn on: raid icons, quest icons, auras, absorbs, the power bar and more appear when they are enabled and disappear when they are not. The Target, Focus and Mouseover pages show the sample in that state, and Buff warnings shows its warnings.\n\nA few pages have a Preview button next to Reset this section for things the sample can't tell from your settings: on the Cast bar page it picks the cast the preview plays, on the Health bar page it picks the sample's enemy type and threat, and on the Elite icon page it picks the badge. They only change the preview, are never saved, and go back to their default when you leave the page.\n\nPages that only matter in the world, like the Behavior pages and Game settings, say so under the preview."
L["The preview plate is shown as the plate under your cursor."] = "The preview plate is shown as the plate under your cursor."
L["The preview plate is shown as your focus."] = "The preview plate is shown as your focus."
L["The preview plate is shown as your target."] = "The preview plate is shown as your target."
L["The profile this character falls back to when no automatic rule applies. Changing it does not replace an automatic override that is active right now."] = "The profile this character falls back to when no automatic rule applies. Changing it does not replace an automatic override that is active right now."
L["The profile this character falls back to when no automatic rule applies. The active profile is the one every page edits."] = "The profile this character falls back to when no automatic rule applies. The active profile is the one every page edits."
L["The resource glows in its own color while it is full, as a cue to spend it."] = "The resource glows in its own color while it is full, as a cue to spend it."
L["The safe state. For a tank: you securely have the enemy, or another tank in your group does. For damage or a healer: the enemy isn't a threat risk for you right now - it doesn't have to be attacking you specifically. Off leaves these enemies with their normal color instead."] = "The safe state. For a tank: you securely have the enemy, or another tank in your group does. For damage or a healer: the enemy isn't a threat risk for you right now - it doesn't have to be attacking you specifically. Off leaves these enemies with their normal color instead."
L["The search box at the top of the window finds any setting by its name or by words in its description. Pick a result to jump to it, even when it sits inside a collapsed section, which opens for you. The setting flashes so you can see it.\n\nWhen you are on the Help page, the same box searches only the help topics instead, so you get help text and not settings. Switch to any other page and it searches settings again."] = "The search box at the top of the window finds any setting by its name or by words in its description. Pick a result to jump to it, even when it sits inside a collapsed section, which opens for you. The setting flashes so you can see it.\n\nWhen you are on the Help page, the same box searches only the help topics instead, so you get help text and not settings. Switch to any other page and it searches settings again."
